.loveandlemons.com/jeanine-donofrio/#person","name":"Jeanine Donofrio","description":"Jeanine Donofrio is a New York Times bestselling cookbook author, recipe developer, and the creator of Love & Lemons. She shares trusted and tested vegetarian recipes for cooks of all levels. Jeanine's work has been featured in Bon Appetit, The Washington Post, Good Morning America, People, and more.","sameAs":["https://www.loveandlemons.com/jeanine-donofrio/","https://www.instagram.com/loveandlemons/","https://www.facebook.com/lovelemonsfood","https://www.pinterest.com/loveandlemons/"],"image":["https://cdn.loveandlemons.com/wp-content/themes/loveandlemons5/images/jeanine720x720.jpg","https://cdn.loveandlemons.com/wp-content/themes/loveandlemons5/images/jeanine720x540.jpg","https://cdn.loveandlemons.com/wp-content/themes/loveandlemons5/images/jeanine720x404.jpg"],"url":"https://www.loveandlemons.com/jeanine-donofrio/"},{"@type":"Person","@id":"https://www.loveandlemons.com/phoebe-moore/#person","name":"Phoebe Moore","description":"Phoebe Moore is the Love & Lemons managing editor and recipe developer. Since joining Love & Lemons in 2018, she has collaborated on three Love & Lemons cookbooks, including Simple Feel Good Food, a New York Times bestseller. She has developed, tested, and edited hundreds of trusted vegetarian recipes for Love & Lemons and has been featured in US News and World Report and New York Magazine.","sameAs":["https://www.loveandlemons.com/phoebe-moore/"],"image":["https://cdn.loveandlemons.com/wp-content/themes/loveandlemons5/images/phoebe720x720.jpg","https://cdn.loveandlemons.com/wp-content/themes/loveandlemons5/images/phoebe720x540.jpg","https://cdn.loveandlemons.com/wp-content/themes/loveandlemons5/images/phoebe720x404.jpg"],"url":"https://www.loveandlemons.com/phoebe-moore/"}],"description":"This breakfast burrito recipe is packed with scrambled eggs, cheese, crispy potatoes, and veggies. It&#039;s one of my favorite meal prep breakfasts. These burritos freeze perfectly!","datePublished":"2021-05-23T09:20:56+00:00","image":["https://cdn.loveandlemons.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/breakfast-burrito-500x500.jpg","https://cdn.loveandlemons.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/breakfast-burrito-500x375.jpg","https://cdn.loveandlemons.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/breakfast-burrito-480x270.jpg","https://cdn.loveandlemons.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/breakfast-burrito.jpg"],"recipeYield":["6"],"prepTime":"PT30M","cookTime":"PT30M","totalTime":"PT60M","recipeIngredient":["1 pound Yukon Gold or yellow potatoes (cut into ¼-inch pieces, or 1 pound frozen diced hash browns, thawed)","Extra-virgin olive oil (for drizzling)","½ teaspoon smoked paprika","¼ teaspoon garlic powder","Sea salt and freshly ground black pepper","1  bell pepper (stemmed, seeded, and diced)","4  green onions (chopped)","1  garlic clove (chopped)","2 cups fresh spinach (chopped)","8  large eggs","6  (12-inch) flour tortillas","1 heaping cup shredded cheddar or Monterey Jack cheese","Salsa (for serving)"],"recipeInstructions":[{"@type":"HowToStep","text":"If using fresh potatoes: Preheat the oven to 425°F and line a baking sheet with parchment paper.","name":"If using fresh potatoes: Preheat the oven to 425°F and line a baking sheet with parchment paper.","url":"https://www.loveandlemons.com/breakfast-burrito/#wprm-recipe-43856-step-0-0"},{"@type":"HowToStep","text":"Place the potatoes on the baking sheet. Drizzle with olive oil and sprinkle with the smoked paprika, garlic powder, and pinches of salt and pepper. Toss to coat and spread evenly on the baking sheet. Roast for 20 to 25 minutes, or until crisp and browned around the edges.","name":"Place the potatoes on the baking sheet. Drizzle with olive oil and sprinkle with the smoked paprika, garlic powder, and pinches of salt and pepper. Toss to coat and spread evenly on the baking sheet. Roast for 20 to 25 minutes, or until crisp and browned around the edges.","url":"https://www.loveandlemons.com/breakfast-burrito/#wprm-recipe-43856-step-0-1"},{"@type":"HowToStep","text":"If using frozen hash browns: Heat a drizzle of olive oil in a large nonstick skillet over medium heat. Add the hash browns in a single layer and cook for 4 to 5 minutes without stirring, or until browned underneath. Add the smoked paprika, garlic powder, and pinches of salt and pepper. Stir to combine, then arrange the potatoes in a single layer again and cook for 4 to 5 minutes, or until well browned. Remove from the pan and set aside.","name":"If using frozen hash browns: Heat a drizzle of olive oil in a large nonstick skillet over medium heat. Add the hash browns in a single layer and cook for 4 to 5 minutes without stirring, or until browned underneath. Add the smoked paprika, garlic powder, and pinches of salt and pepper. Stir to combine, then arrange the potatoes in a single layer again and cook for 4 to 5 minutes, or until well browned. Remove from the pan and set aside.","url":"https://www.loveandlemons.com/breakfast-burrito/#wprm-recipe-43856-step-0-2"},{"@type":"HowToStep","text":"Return the pan to medium heat and add another drizzle of olive oil. Add the bell pepper, green onions, garlic, and pinches of salt and pepper. Cook, stirring occasionally, for 5 minutes, or until softened. Add the spinach and cook until wilted. Remove from the pan and set aside.","name":"Return the pan to medium heat and add another drizzle of olive oil. Add the bell pepper, green onions, garlic, and pinches of salt and pepper. Cook, stirring occasionally, for 5 minutes, or until softened. Add the spinach and cook until wilted. Remove from the pan and set aside.","url":"https://www.loveandlemons.com/breakfast-burrito/#wprm-recipe-43856-step-0-3"},{"@type":"HowToStep","text":"In a medium bowl, whisk the eggs with a pinch of salt and several grinds of pepper. Return the pan to medium-low heat and pour in the eggs. Stir to scramble, cooking until just set. Remove from the pan and set aside.","name":"In a medium bowl, whisk the eggs with a pinch of salt and several grinds of pepper. Return the pan to medium-low heat and pour in the eggs. Stir to scramble, cooking until just set. Remove from the pan and set aside.","url":"https://www.loveandlemons.com/breakfast-burrito/#wprm-recipe-43856-step-0-4"},{"@type":"HowToStep","text":"To assemble the burritos, fill each tortilla with some of the eggs, potatoes, pepper mixture, and cheese. Fold and roll to close.","name":"To assemble the burritos, fill each tortilla with some of the eggs, potatoes, pepper mixture, and cheese. Fold and roll to close.","url":"https://www.loveandlemons.com/breakfast-burrito/#wprm-recipe-43856-step-0-5"},{"@type":"HowToStep","text":"If enjoying right away, lightly brush a large skillet with olive oil and heat over medium-low heat. Working in batches if necessary, place the burritos in the pan and toast for 2 to 4 minutes per side, or until browned and crisp. Serve with salsa for dipping.","name":"If enjoying right away, lightly brush a large skillet with olive oil and heat over medium-low heat. Working in batches if necessary, place the burritos in the pan and toast for 2 to 4 minutes per side, or until browned and crisp. Serve with salsa for dipping.","url":"https://www.loveandlemons.com/breakfast-burrito/#wprm-recipe-43856-step-0-6"},{"@type":"HowToStep","text":"If freezing, wrap tightly in foil and freeze for up to 3 months. To reheat frozen burritos, unwrap the foil and wrap loosely in a paper towel or kitchen towel. Microwave for 3 to 4 minutes, flipping halfway, or until soft and thawed in the middle. Microwave for another 2 to 3 minutes to fully heat the burrito through, or if desired, crisp the tortilla on the stovetop using the method above. (You can also crisp them in an air fryer or toaster oven for 4 to 6 minutes. Flip halfway through.)","name":"If freezing, wrap tightly in foil and freeze for up to 3 months. To reheat frozen burritos, unwrap the foil and wrap loosely in a paper towel or kitchen towel. Microwave for 3 to 4 minutes, flipping halfway, or until soft and thawed in the middle. Microwave for another 2 to 3 minutes to fully heat the burrito through, or if desired, crisp the tortilla on the stovetop using the method above. (You can also crisp them in an air fryer or toaster oven for 4 to 6 minutes. Flip halfway through.)","url":"https://www.loveandlemons.com/breakfast-burrito/#wprm-recipe-43856-step-0-7"}],"aggregateRating":{"@type":"AggregateRating","ratingValue":"4.92","ratingCount":"24","reviewCount":13},"recipeCategory":["Breakfast"],"recipeCuisine":["American","Mexican","Tex Mex"],"keywords":"breakfast burrito, breakfast burrito recipe, breakfast burritos, breakfast burritos recipe","nutrition":{"@type":"NutritionInformation","servingSize":"1 burrito","calories":"338 kcal","carbohydrateContent":"46 g","proteinContent":"15 g","fatContent":"11 g","saturatedFatContent":"4 g","transFatContent":"0.02 g","cholesterolContent":"218 mg","sodiumContent":"589 mg","fiberContent":"5 g","sugarContent":"4 g","unsaturatedFatContent":"6 g"},"@id":"https://www.loveandlemons.com/breakfast-burrito/#recipe","review":[{"@type":"Review","datePublished":"2025-07-07 09:23:13","reviewBody":"Oh my God that looks so good. It's a great way  to make a breakfast. I'm definitely gonna give it a try. I hope my husband likes it.","reviewRating":{"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":5},"author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Hunter."}},{"@type":"Review","datePublished":"2025-05-05 17:26:07","reviewBody":"Breakfast burrito is realy best breakfast i like it.","reviewRating":{"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":5},"author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Riaz"}},{"@type":"Review","datePublished":"2022-06-12 18:23:44","reviewBody":"These were so tasty &amp; filling. Especially the cilantro lime dressing. The recipe was a bit time consuming, but it was worth it. Next time, I'll prepare some of the side dishes the day before, to save time. Thank you for sharing.","reviewRating":{"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":5},"author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Angela"}},{"@type":"Review","datePublished":"2022-03-14 18:31:45","reviewBody":"Fantastic burrito recipe. Very clear and coming with amazing pictures. Thanks for sharing.","reviewRating":{"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":5},"author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Fernando Alerts"}},{"@type":"Review","datePublished":"2021-05-24 16:08:51","reviewBody":"Finally, a healthy breakfast burrito.   Thank you!","reviewRating":{"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":5},"author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Julie"}},{"@type":"Review","datePublished":"2020-05-01 22:56:51","reviewBody":"My mum and I made these breakfast burritos for the family's brunch. They were absolutely delicious! We particularly enjoyed the cilantro lime dressing :)","reviewRating":{"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":5},"author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Ashley"}},{"@type":"Review","datePublished":"2020-04-20 12:18:15","reviewBody":"these were amazing!","reviewRating":{"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":5},"author":{"@type":"Person","name":"jackie"}},{"@type":"Review","datePublished":"2020-01-30 11:21:12","reviewBody":"So so tasty! We made these with my family (who are all healthy eaters) and they were a big hit! We laid out all the fillings and had people build their own burrito! A big hit!","reviewRating":{"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":5},"author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Bri Schneider"}},{"@type":"Review","datePublished":"2019-12-19 11:53:38","reviewBody":"It's Yummy. My Sister and Brother Love It. Thanks For Sharing.","reviewRating":{"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":5},"author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Prachiti"}}]}]}</script> <link
