class="entry-header entry-header-single"><h1 class="entry-title">
Breakfast Burrito</h1></header><div
class="entry-content entry-content-single"><p
class=first-sentence>This easy breakfast burrito recipe is filled with scrambled eggs, crispy potatoes, veggies, and cheese. It's a delicious meal prep breakfast!</p><div
class=entry-meta><div
class="author-byline first-line">
<a
href=/jeanine-donofrio/ ><img
width=48 height=48 src=https://cdn.loveandlemons.com/wp-content/themes/loveandlemons5/images/jeanine96x96v1.jpg></a>
<a
href=/jeanine-donofrio/ >Jeanine Donofrio</a></div><div
class="author-byline first-line">
<a
href=/phoebe-moore/ ><img
width=48 height=48 src=https://cdn.loveandlemons.com/wp-content/themes/loveandlemons5/images/phoebe96x96v1.jpg></a>
<a
href=/phoebe-moore/ >Phoebe Moore</a></div><div
class="updated-date first-line">Updated Aug 14, 2026</div><div
class=lnl-tags>
<a
href=#wprm-recipe-container-43856>Jump to recipe</a></div></div><div
class=under-h2></div><div
class=pin-hidden-image-container>
<img
src="data:image/svg+xml;base64,PHN2ZyB4bWxucz0naHR0cDovL3d3dy53My5vcmcvMjAwMC9zdmcnIHdpZHRoPScwJyBoZWlnaHQ9JzAnPjwvc3ZnPg==" data-pin-description data-pin-media=https://cdn.loveandlemons.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/Breakfast-Burrito-1.png></div><p>
<span
class="pibfi_pinterest ">
<img
fetchpriority=high decoding=async class="alignnone wp-image-95189 size-full" src=https://cdn.loveandlemons.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/breakfast-burrito-recipe.jpg alt="Breakfast burrito" style="aspect-ratio:1740 / 2237" width=1740 height=2237 data-pin-description="This breakfast burrito recipe is an easy, healthy breakfast that's great for meal prep! It's filled with scrambled eggs, crispy potatoes, fresh veggies, and cheese. I love to freeze these for busy mornings." srcset="https://cdn.loveandlemons.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/breakfast-burrito-recipe.jpg 1740w, https://cdn.loveandlemons.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/breakfast-burrito-recipe-233x300.jpg 233w, https://cdn.loveandlemons.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/breakfast-burrito-recipe-796x1024.jpg 796w, https://cdn.loveandlemons.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/breakfast-burrito-recipe-78x100.jpg 78w, https://cdn.loveandlemons.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/breakfast-burrito-recipe-580x746.jpg 580w, https://cdn.loveandlemons.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/breakfast-burrito-recipe-1160x1491.jpg 1160w" sizes="(min-width: 960px) 580px, 100vw" data-pin-url=https://www.loveandlemons.com/breakfast-burrito/ >
<span
class=xc_pin onclick="pin_this(event, 'http://pinterest.com/pin/create/button/?url=https://www.loveandlemons.com/breakfast-burrito/&media=https://www.loveandlemons.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/breakfast-burrito-recipe.jpg&description=This+breakfast+burrito+recipe+is+an+easy%2C+healthy+breakfast+that%27s+great+for+meal+prep%21+It%27s+filled+with+scrambled+eggs%2C+crispy+potatoes%2C+fresh+veggies%2C+and+cheese.+I+love+to+freeze+these+for+busy+mornings.')">
</span>
</span></p><p><strong>Meet my favorite breakfast burrito recipe!</strong> These easy, cheesy breakfast burritos are loaded with fluffy scrambled eggs, crispy potatoes, fresh veggies, and melty cheddar cheese. I love to make them on lazy weekend mornings. Jack and I eat two right away, and I stash the rest in the freezer for easy meals during the week. They reheat perfectly for a quick grab-and-go breakfast or lunch. Spice things up by serving them with a side of your favorite <a
href=https://www.loveandlemons.com/homemade-salsa-recipe/ >salsa</a> or hot sauce!</p><div
class=callout><h2>Why You&#8217;ll Love This Recipe</h2><ul>
<li><strong>It&#8217;s freezer-friendly. </strong>These breakfast burritos freeze well for up to 3 months! They&#8217;re easy to thaw in the microwave (and crisp up on the stovetop, if you like) for a healthy, hearty breakfast packed with protein and veggies.</li>
<li><strong>It&#8217;s easy to customize. </strong>Don&#8217;t see your favorite burrito filling here? Feel free to add it in! Avocado, veggie breakfast sausage, <a
href=https://www.loveandlemons.com/pickled-red-onions/ >pickled onions</a>, and more are fantastic in this recipe.</li>
<li><strong>Pick your potato. </strong>I usually roast my own breakfast potatoes for this recipe. But in a pinch, diced frozen hash browns work just as well and save some time. I&#8217;m sharing instructions for both options in the recipe!</li></ul></div><p>
<span
class="pibfi_pinterest ">
<img
