class=xc_pin onclick="pin_this(event, 'http://pinterest.com/pin/create/button/?url=https://www.loveandlemons.com/breakfast-burrito/&media=https://www.loveandlemons.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/breakfast-burrito-meal-prep.jpg&description=This+breakfast+burrito+recipe+is+an+easy%2C+healthy+breakfast+that%27s+great+for+meal+prep%21+It%27s+filled+with+scrambled+eggs%2C+crispy+potatoes%2C+fresh+veggies%2C+and+cheese.+I+love+to+freeze+these+for+busy+mornings.')">
</span>
</span></p><h2>Breakfast Burrito Ingredients</h2><p>Here&#8217;s what you&#8217;ll need to make this breakfast burrito recipe:</p><ul>
<li><strong>Large flour tortillas </strong>&#8211; In the store, look for 12-inch or larger tortillas. Often, they’ll be labeled as “Burrito-Size.” These tortillas are the easiest to tuck and roll around all the yummy fillings.</li>
<li><strong>Yukon Gold potatoes or diced frozen hash browns</strong> &#8211; You&#8217;ll roast the potatoes in the oven or crisp up the hash browns on the stove.</li>
<li><strong>Garlic powder and smoked paprika</strong> &#8211; They fill the potatoes with smoky, savory flavor.</li>
<li><strong>Eggs </strong>&#8211; Is it really a breakfast burrito without them? I scramble them to add creamy, fluffy texture to the burritos.</li>
<li><strong>Shredded cheddar or Monterey Jack cheese</strong> &#8211; For richness and tangy flavor.</li>
<li><strong>Spinach and bell pepper </strong>&#8211; They pack these burritos with a veggie punch. Feel free to use any color of bell pepper here. I like a mix of red and green.</li>
<li><strong>Green onions and garlic </strong>&#8211; For fresh, onion-y flavor.</li>
<li><strong>Extra-virgin olive oil </strong>&#8211; For cooking the eggs and potatoes.</li>
<li><strong>And salt and pepper</strong> &#8211; To make all the flavors pop!</li></ul><p><em>Find the complete recipe with measurements below.</em></p><p>
<span
class="pibfi_pinterest ">
<img
loading=lazy  decoding=async class="alignnone wp-image-95190 size-full" src=https://cdn.loveandlemons.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/breakfast-burrito-recipes.jpg alt="Cheese, scrambled eggs, roasted potatoes, and veggies in center of large flour tortilla" width=1740 height=2420 data-pin-description="This breakfast burrito recipe is an easy, healthy breakfast that's great for meal prep! It's filled with scrambled eggs, crispy potatoes, fresh veggies, and cheese. I love to freeze these for busy mornings." srcset="https://cdn.loveandlemons.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/breakfast-burrito-recipes.jpg 1740w, https://cdn.loveandlemons.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/breakfast-burrito-recipes-216x300.jpg 216w, https://cdn.loveandlemons.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/breakfast-burrito-recipes-736x1024.jpg 736w, https://cdn.loveandlemons.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/breakfast-burrito-recipes-72x100.jpg 72w, https://cdn.loveandlemons.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/breakfast-burrito-recipes-580x807.jpg 580w, https://cdn.loveandlemons.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/breakfast-burrito-recipes-1160x1613.jpg 1160w" sizes="(min-width: 960px) 580px, 100vw" data-pin-url=https://www.loveandlemons.com/breakfast-burrito/ >
<span
class=xc_pin onclick="pin_this(event, 'http://pinterest.com/pin/create/button/?url=https://www.loveandlemons.com/breakfast-burrito/&media=https://www.loveandlemons.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/breakfast-burrito-recipes.jpg&description=This+breakfast+burrito+recipe+is+an+easy%2C+healthy+breakfast+that%27s+great+for+meal+prep%21+It%27s+filled+with+scrambled+eggs%2C+crispy+potatoes%2C+fresh+veggies%2C+and+cheese.+I+love+to+freeze+these+for+busy+mornings.')">
</span>
</span></p><h2>How to Make a Breakfast Burrito</h2><p>This recipe has four simple steps:</p><ol>
<li><strong>Prep the potatoes. </strong><em>Tip: </em>If you&#8217;d like to break up some of the burrito prep, you can cook the potatoes a day or two ahead. Store them in an airtight container in the refrigerator until you&#8217;re ready to assemble!</li>
<li><strong>Chop and sauté the veggies. </strong></li>
<li><strong>Scramble the eggs.</strong></li>
<li><strong>Assemble the burritos. </strong></li></ol><div
class=callout><p>A few tips for assembly:</p><ul>
<li><strong>Lay your fillings in a (relatively) narrow strip on the center of the tortilla.</strong> If you spread the ingredients out too much, you won’t be able to get the tortilla over and around them.</li>
<li><strong>Tuck in the sides of the tortilla first.</strong> Then, fold the tortilla over the fillings and roll it closed. I’ve found this “tuck &amp; roll” method to be the most effective for tightly packing the filling into the tortilla.</li></ul></div><p>
<span
class="pibfi_pinterest ">
<img
loading=lazy decoding=async class="alignnone wp-image-95192 size-full" src=https://cdn.loveandlemons.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/high-protein-breakfast-burrito.jpg alt="Hands rolling breakfast burrito closed" width=1740 height=1762 data-pin-description="This breakfast burrito recipe is an easy, healthy breakfast that's great for meal prep! It's filled with scrambled eggs, crispy potatoes, fresh veggies, and cheese. I love to freeze these for busy mornings." srcset="https://cdn.loveandlemons.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/high-protein-breakfast-burrito.jpg 1740w, https://cdn.loveandlemons.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/high-protein-breakfast-burrito-296x300.jpg 296w, https://cdn.loveandlemons.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/high-protein-breakfast-burrito-1011x1024.jpg 1011w, https://cdn.loveandlemons.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/high-protein-breakfast-burrito-100x100.jpg 100w, https://cdn.loveandlemons.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/high-protein-breakfast-burrito-580x587.jpg 580w, https://cdn.loveandlemons.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/high-protein-breakfast-burrito-1160x1175.jpg 1160w" sizes="auto, (min-width: 960px) 580px, 100vw" data-pin-url=https://www.loveandlemons.com/breakfast-burrito/ >
<span
class=xc_pin onclick="pin_this(event, 'http://pinterest.com/pin/create/button/?url=https://www.loveandlemons.com/breakfast-burrito/&media=https://www.loveandlemons.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/high-protein-breakfast-burrito.jpg&description=This+breakfast+burrito+recipe+is+an+easy%2C+healthy+breakfast+that%27s+great+for+meal+prep%21+It%27s+filled+with+scrambled+eggs%2C+crispy+potatoes%2C+fresh+veggies%2C+and+cheese.+I+love+to+freeze+these+for+busy+mornings.')">
</span>
</span></p><h2>How to Make Ahead and Freeze</h2><p><strong>To freeze:</strong></p><ul>
<li>Fully assemble the burritos and wrap each one in foil.</li>
<li>Store in an airtight container or bag in the freezer for up to 3 months.</li></ul><p><strong>To reheat:</strong></p><ul>
<li>Unwrap the foil, then wrap the burrito in a paper towel or kitchen towel.</li>
<li>Microwave for 3 to 4 minutes, flipping halfway, until thawed.</li>
<li><em>Option 1:</em> Microwave for another 2 to 3 minutes to heat the burrito through.</li>
<li><em>Option 2:</em> Crisp the tortilla! Heat a drizzle of olive oil in a skillet over medium heat. Cook the thawed burrito on each side until golden brown and lightly crisp.</li></ul><div
class=callout><h2>What to Serve with Breakfast Burritos</h2><p>If you ask me, any burrito (breakfast or otherwise) is best with a tasty sauce for dipping. Here are a few I love with this recipe:</p><ul>
<li><a
href=https://www.loveandlemons.com/homemade-salsa-recipe/ >Homemade Salsa</a></li>
<li><a
href=https://www.loveandlemons.com/tomatillo-salsa-verde/ >Tomatillo Salsa Verde</a></li>
<li><a
href=https://www.loveandlemons.com/chipotle-sauce/ >Chipotle Sauce</a></li>
<li><a
href=https://www.loveandlemons.com/cilantro-lime-dressing/ >Cilantro Lime Dressing</a></li></ul><p>A side of <a
href=https://www.loveandlemons.com/guacamole-recipe/ >guacamole</a>, <a
href=https://www.loveandlemons.com/pico-de-gallo/ >pico de gallo</a>, or sour cream would be great too!</p></div><h4>
